			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20022015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">
				Folly is 
				<crossref let="d" cid="c20022015.29">
				</crossref>
				bound up, 
				<crossref let="e" cid="c20022015.30">
				</crossref>
				in the heart of a child, but the rod of discipline drives it far from him.
				<note nid="n20022015.15">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20022016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">
				Whoever oppresses 
				<crossref let="f" cid="c20022016.31">
				</crossref>
				the poor, 
				<crossref let="g" cid="c20022016.32">
				</crossref>
				to increase his own wealth, or gives to the rich, will only come to poverty. Words of the Wise
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20022017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">
				Incline your 
				<crossref let="h" cid="c20022017.33">
				</crossref>
				ear, and, 
				<crossref let="i" cid="c20022017.34">
				</crossref>
